It seems that all three work, but in a slightly different manner. The
bullwhip is least preferable, because you need a means of levitation in
addition.  But if you have that, it can work pretty fast.

Bullwhip: Levitate *above* the pit, apply the whip ">".  It will wrap
around the object you are trying to recover, but more often than not
will slip loose again (I did this at dexterity 23, so for low enough
dexterity, it may not work at all.  It appears, your dexterity must be >
14.)

Grappling hook: No need for levitation. Stand on one of the squares next
to the pit and apply the hook in the appropriate direction (not > !).
Success rate is not hundred percent and you may be yanked towards the
pit, which is not a problem as a flying monster.  Eventually, it will
get the object out of the pit (dependence on dexterity?).

Fishing pole:  No need for levitation. Stand on one of the squares next
to the pit and apply the pole in the appropriate direction (not > !). In
my case, this worked faster than the hook, and I never got yanked toward
the pit, but it is possible to hurt one's foot.

